        "acip": "LONG 'KHRID DANG 'DRA BA'I DGE BA'I BSHES GNYEN BSTEN SKABS KYANG SDIG DANG MA 'DRES PA'I NGAL DUB KYI NGAN LAS JI 'DRA ZHIG BYED DGOS PA BYUNG YANG GZHAN LA DKA' SPYAD BYAS RABS KYI YUS MI BDO BAR MA ZAD,",
        "wylie": "long 'khrid dang 'dra ba'i dge ba'i bshes gnyen bsten skabs kyang sdig dang ma 'dres pa'i ngal dub kyi ngan las ji 'dra zhig byed dgos pa byung yang gzhan la dka' spyad byas rabs kyi yus mi bdo bar ma zad",
        "english": "My spiritual Friend is here to lead the blind; and in my service of him or her I am obliged to do anything required of me, no matter how exhausting, no matter how distasteful--so long as nothing morally wrong is involved.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"C16\", \"acip\": \"LONG 'KHRID DANG 'DRA BA'I DGE BA'I BSHES GNYEN BSTEN SKABS KYANG SDIG DANG MA 'DRES PA'I NGAL DUB KYI NGAN LAS JI 'DRA ZHIG BYED DGOS PA BYUNG YANG GZHAN LA DKA' SPYAD BYAS RABS KYI YUS MI BDO BAR MA ZAD,\", \"wylie\": \"long 'khrid dang 'dra ba'i dge ba'i bshes gnyen bsten skabs kyang sdig dang ma 'dres pa'i ngal dub kyi ngan las ji 'dra zhig byed dgos pa byung yang gzhan la dka' spyad byas rabs kyi yus mi bdo bar ma zad\", \"english\": \"My spiritual Friend is here to lead the blind; and in my service of him or her I am obliged to do anything required of me, no matter how exhausting, no matter how distasteful--so long as nothing morally wrong is involved.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 33616,
        "course": "EM",
        "seq": 908,
        "acip": "DE YANG CHOS MTHUN GYI RNYED PA LEGS RNYED CIG DGOS KYI, LOG 'TSO DANG SDIG ZAS PHUL BA'I RNYED PA BYUNG YANG NYES RNYED YIN PAR BLA MAS GSUNGS PAS LEGS PAR RNYED CES PA SDIG CHE BA DANG MA 'DRES PA'I ZAS RNYED SLA BA DGOS,",
        "wylie": "de yang chos mthun gyi rnyed pa legs rnyed cig dgos kyi, log 'tsho dang sdig zas phul ba'i rnyed pa byung yang nyes rnyed yin par bla mas gsungs pas legs par rnyed ces pa sdig che ba dang ma 'dres pa'i zas rnyed sla ba dgos",
        "english": "The supplies that we use for our spiritual practice should be good in another sense: they should be obtained in a proper way. As the teachers have said, “Even if someone offers us a gift of food for our practice periods, but that food has been obtained through some wrong kind of occupation or other bad deeds; then actually we've been offered a karmic debt, and not a gift.” And so when we say that you need to find a place where necessities can easily be found, we are talking about a place where you can find support that is not mixed up with any kind of terrible bad deeds.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"EM\", \"acip\": \"DE YANG CHOS MTHUN GYI RNYED PA LEGS RNYED CIG DGOS KYI, LOG 'TSO DANG SDIG ZAS PHUL BA'I RNYED PA BYUNG YANG NYES RNYED YIN PAR BLA MAS GSUNGS PAS LEGS PAR RNYED CES PA SDIG CHE BA DANG MA 'DRES PA'I ZAS RNYED SLA BA DGOS,\", \"wylie\": \"de yang chos mthun gyi rnyed pa legs rnyed cig dgos kyi, log 'tsho dang sdig zas phul ba'i rnyed pa byung yang nyes rnyed yin par bla mas gsungs pas legs par rnyed ces pa sdig che ba dang ma 'dres pa'i zas rnyed sla ba dgos\", \"english\": \"The supplies that we use for our spiritual practice should be good in another sense: they should be obtained in a proper way. As the teachers have said, “Even if someone offers us a gift of food for our practice periods, but that food has been obtained through some wrong kind of occupation or other bad deeds; then actually we've been offered a karmic debt, and not a gift.” And so when we say that you need to find a place where necessities can easily be found, we are talking about a place where you can find support that is not mixed up with any kind of terrible bad deeds.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 24211,
        "course": "GIE",
        "seq": 699,
        "acip": "MA 'DRES PA'I DRAN PA NYER GZHAG GSUM,",
        "wylie": "ma 'dres pa'i dran pa nyer gzhag gsum",
        "english": "We continue on to the three kinds of close awareness which are unblended.  These are said to be “unblended” in that they are unique.  First comes (1) a close awareness that we should eliminate, within ourselves, any attachment to disciples who listen to our teachings with respect; then (2) a close awareness that we should eliminate, within ourselves, any form of feeling offended by disciples who listen to our teachings, but who show us disrespect; and (3) a close awareness which is devoid of either of these feelings, of attachment or offense.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"GIE\", \"acip\": \"MA 'DRES PA'I DRAN PA NYER GZHAG GSUM,\", \"wylie\": \"ma 'dres pa'i dran pa nyer gzhag gsum\", \"english\": \"We continue on to the three kinds of close awareness which are unblended.  These are said to be “unblended” in that they are unique.  First comes (1) a close awareness that we should eliminate, within ourselves, any attachment to disciples who listen to our teachings with respect; then (2) a close awareness that we should eliminate, within ourselves, any form of feeling offended by disciples who listen to our teachings, but who show us disrespect; and (3) a close awareness which is devoid of either of these feelings, of attachment or offense.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 24772,
        "course": "GIE",
        "seq": 1260,
        "acip": "[E165] BZHI PA MA 'DRES PA'I RNAM PA NI,",
        "wylie": "[e165] bzhi pa ma 'dres pa'i rnam pa ni",
        "english": "This brings us to the fourth sub-group here: the unmixed qualities.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"GIE\", \"acip\": \"[E165] BZHI PA MA 'DRES PA'I RNAM PA NI,\", \"wylie\": \"[e165] bzhi pa ma 'dres pa'i rnam pa ni\", \"english\": \"This brings us to the fourth sub-group here: the unmixed qualities.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 27173,
        "course": "GK",
        "seq": 225,
        "acip": "MA 'DRES PA'I MA RIG PA MED PAR THAL, DE 'PHAGS LAM MA THOB BAR DU RGYUN MI 'CHAD DU 'JUG PAS 'JUG SHES KYI 'KHOR DU MI 'BYUNG, NYON YID KYI 'KHOR DU 'BYUNG TSUL MED PA'I PHYIR, /1\\",
        "wylie": "ma 'dres pa'i ma rig pa med par thal, de 'phags lam ma thob bar du rgyun mi 'chad du 'jug pas 'jug shes kyi 'khor du mi 'byung, nyon yid kyi 'khor du 'byung tshul med pa'i phyir, /1\\",
        "english": "Are you saying then that there is no such thing as a state of misunderstanding which is not admixed? Why do you say that? Because this state of misunderstanding is something that engages in an unbroken stream, up to the point that we finally reach the state of a realized being.  As such it cannot occur as an adjunct to those states of consciousness which engage [intermittently] in their respective objects; nor, according to you, can it occur as an adjunct to a negative consciousness. Second reason not to deny negative consciousness",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"GK\", \"acip\": \"MA 'DRES PA'I MA RIG PA MED PAR THAL, DE 'PHAGS LAM MA THOB BAR DU RGYUN MI 'CHAD DU 'JUG PAS 'JUG SHES KYI 'KHOR DU MI 'BYUNG, NYON YID KYI 'KHOR DU 'BYUNG TSUL MED PA'I PHYIR, /1\\\\\", \"wylie\": \"ma 'dres pa'i ma rig pa med par thal, de 'phags lam ma thob bar du rgyun mi 'chad du 'jug pas 'jug shes kyi 'khor du mi 'byung, nyon yid kyi 'khor du 'byung tshul med pa'i phyir, /1\\\\\", \"english\": \"Are you saying then that there is no such thing as a state of misunderstanding which is not admixed? Why do you say that? Because this state of misunderstanding is something that engages in an unbroken stream, up to the point that we finally reach the state of a realized being.  As such it cannot occur as an adjunct to those states of consciousness which engage [intermittently] in their respective objects; nor, according to you, can it occur as an adjunct to a negative consciousness. Second reason not to deny negative consciousness\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 27960,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 641,
        "acip": "GNYIS PA SA GNYIS PA DRI MA MED PA BSHAD PA LA LNGA, SA 'DIR TSUL KHRIMS YONGS SU DAG PAR BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI BSNGAGS PA BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI MI MTHUN PHYOGS DANG MA 'DRES PA'I DPE BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI PHAR PHYIN GYI DBYE BA BSTAN PA DANG, SA'I YON TAN BRJOD PA'I SGO NAS MJUG BSDU BA'O,,",
        "wylie": "gnyis pa sa gnyis pa dri ma med pa bshad pa la lnga, sa 'dir tshul khrims yongs su dag par bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi bsngags pa bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi mi mthun phyogs dang ma 'dres pa'i dpe bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi phar phyin gyi dbye ba bstan pa dang, sa'i yon tan brjod pa'i sgo nas mjug bsdu ba'o",
        "english": "Here is our second division from above, which is an explanation of the second bodhisattva level: Immaculate. This has five parts of its own: a presentation about how, at this level, ones ethical life is completely pure; a presentation of the praises of an ethical life; the presentation of a metaphor to describe how—at this level—ones ethical life is beyond any adulteration by the things that could work against it; a presentation of the divisions of the perfection of an ethical life; and a concluding summary of this level, accomplished by describing its high qualities.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"GNYIS PA SA GNYIS PA DRI MA MED PA BSHAD PA LA LNGA, SA 'DIR TSUL KHRIMS YONGS SU DAG PAR BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI BSNGAGS PA BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI MI MTHUN PHYOGS DANG MA 'DRES PA'I DPE BSTAN PA DANG, TSUL KHRIMS KYI PHAR PHYIN GYI DBYE BA BSTAN PA DANG, SA'I YON TAN BRJOD PA'I SGO NAS MJUG BSDU BA'O,,\", \"wylie\": \"gnyis pa sa gnyis pa dri ma med pa bshad pa la lnga, sa 'dir tshul khrims yongs su dag par bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi bsngags pa bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi mi mthun phyogs dang ma 'dres pa'i dpe bstan pa dang, tshul khrims kyi phar phyin gyi dbye ba bstan pa dang, sa'i yon tan brjod pa'i sgo nas mjug bsdu ba'o\", \"english\": \"Here is our second division from above, which is an explanation of the second bodhisattva level: Immaculate. This has five parts of its own: a presentation about how, at this level, ones ethical life is completely pure; a presentation of the praises of an ethical life; the presentation of a metaphor to describe how—at this level—ones ethical life is beyond any adulteration by the things that could work against it; a presentation of the divisions of the perfection of an ethical life; and a concluding summary of this level, accomplished by describing its high qualities.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 31237,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 3918,
        "acip": "SANGS RGYAS KYI CHOS NI, MA 'DRES PA BCU DANG BRGYAD DU GANG 'DOD PA DE DAG GZHAN GYIS MI 'PHROGS PA'I RANG GI MTSAN NYID CAN TE, RGYU MTSAN GANG GI PHYIR NA STON PA LA MA 'DRES PA'I MI MTHUN PHYOGS 'KHRUL PA SOGS MI MNGA' BAS DE RNAMS KYIS GLAGS MED PA NYID KYIS MI 'PHROGS PA STE, THUB PAR MI NUS PA DE'I PHYIR RO,,",
        "wylie": "sangs rgyas kyi chos ni, ma 'dres pa bcu dang brgyad du gang 'dod pa de dag gzhan gyis mi 'phrogs pa'i rang gi mtshan nyid can te, rgyu mtshan gang gi phyir na ston pa la ma 'dres pa'i mi mthun phyogs 'khrul pa sogs mi mnga' bas de rnams kyis glags med pa nyid kyis mi 'phrogs pa ste, thub par mi nus pa de'i phyir ro",
        "english": "The Dharma of the Buddhas, which we assert has those 18 qualities of being unmixed, has an own quality that it cannot be stolen off by others. The reason why this is true is that the Teacher has no nature of being mixed in with things like error, or ideas that would contradict their positions. As such, their teachings cannot be “stolen off,” or defeated—for that simple reason that they cannot be defeated.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"SANGS RGYAS KYI CHOS NI, MA 'DRES PA BCU DANG BRGYAD DU GANG 'DOD PA DE DAG GZHAN GYIS MI 'PHROGS PA'I RANG GI MTSAN NYID CAN TE, RGYU MTSAN GANG GI PHYIR NA STON PA LA MA 'DRES PA'I MI MTHUN PHYOGS 'KHRUL PA SOGS MI MNGA' BAS DE RNAMS KYIS GLAGS MED PA NYID KYIS MI 'PHROGS PA STE, THUB PAR MI NUS PA DE'I PHYIR RO,,\", \"wylie\": \"sangs rgyas kyi chos ni, ma 'dres pa bcu dang brgyad du gang 'dod pa de dag gzhan gyis mi 'phrogs pa'i rang gi mtshan nyid can te, rgyu mtshan gang gi phyir na ston pa la ma 'dres pa'i mi mthun phyogs 'khrul pa sogs mi mnga' bas de rnams kyis glags med pa nyid kyis mi 'phrogs pa ste, thub par mi nus pa de'i phyir ro\", \"english\": \"The Dharma of the Buddhas, which we assert has those 18 qualities of being unmixed, has an own quality that it cannot be stolen off by others. The reason why this is true is that the Teacher has no nature of being mixed in with things like error, or ideas that would contradict their positions. As such, their teachings cannot be “stolen off,” or defeated—for that simple reason that they cannot be defeated.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 31241,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 3922,
        "acip": "MA 'DRES PA'I NGES TSIG NI CHOS DE RNAMS SANGS RGYAS KHO NA'I RTEN LA YOD KYI, RTEN GZHAN LA MED PAS RTEN MA 'DRES PA'O,,",
        "wylie": "ma 'dres pa'i nges tshig ni chos de rnams sangs rgyas kho na'i rten la yod kyi, rten gzhan la med pas rten ma 'dres pa'o",
        "english": "Why are these 18 called “unmixed”? The point is that these are possessed in the person only of beings who are Buddhas, and are unmixed in the person of other subjects.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"MA 'DRES PA'I NGES TSIG NI CHOS DE RNAMS SANGS RGYAS KHO NA'I RTEN LA YOD KYI, RTEN GZHAN LA MED PAS RTEN MA 'DRES PA'O,,\", \"wylie\": \"ma 'dres pa'i nges tshig ni chos de rnams sangs rgyas kho na'i rten la yod kyi, rten gzhan la med pas rten ma 'dres pa'o\", \"english\": \"Why are these 18 called “unmixed”? The point is that these are possessed in the person only of beings who are Buddhas, and are unmixed in the person of other subjects.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 31904,
        "course": "ILL",
        "seq": 4585,
        "acip": "c1) TSUL KHRIMS KYI MI MTHUN PHYOGS DANG MA 'DRES PA'I DPE BSTAN PA, [v. II.8]",
        "wylie": "c1) tshul khrims kyi mi mthun phyogs dang ma 'dres pa'i dpe bstan pa, [v. ii.8]",
        "english": "The presentation of a metaphor to describe how—at this level—ones ethical life is beyond any adulteration by the things that could work against it",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"ILL\", \"acip\": \"c1) TSUL KHRIMS KYI MI MTHUN PHYOGS DANG MA 'DRES PA'I DPE BSTAN PA, [v. II.8]\", \"wylie\": \"c1) tshul khrims kyi mi mthun phyogs dang ma 'dres pa'i dpe bstan pa, [v. ii.8]\", \"english\": \"The presentation of a metaphor to describe how—at this level—ones ethical life is beyond any adulteration by the things that could work against it\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 34751,
        "course": "P6",
        "seq": 48,
        "acip": "RNAM PAR SUN 'BYIN PA'I STOBS NI 'GYOD SEMS BYED PA STE DPER NA MI BZHIS, DUG DANG 'DRES PA'I ZAS MNYAM DU ZOS NAS GCIG SHI GCIG SHI LA KHAD DU GYUR GCIG NA NAS YOD NA CIG SHOS MA NA PA DE LA 'GYOD PA GTAN MI BZOD PA 'ONG BA LTAR",
        "wylie": "rnam par sun 'byin pa'i stobs ni 'gyod sems byed pa ste dper na mi bzhis, dug dang 'dres pa'i zas mnyam du zos nas gcig shi gcig shi la khad du gyur gcig na nas yod na cig shos ma na pa de la 'gyod pa gtan mi bzod pa 'ong ba ltar",
        "english": "The \"power of destruction\" refers to an emotion of regret. Imagine for example that four people have been sitting around a table eating the same dish mixed with some deadly poison. Now one of them has already fallen over and died. Another is taking his last breath. The third is writhing in agony. The fourth hasn't started feeling the effects yet. Think though of the unbearable regret that he has already begun to feel about eating that particular dish.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"P6\", \"acip\": \"RNAM PAR SUN 'BYIN PA'I STOBS NI 'GYOD SEMS BYED PA STE DPER NA MI BZHIS, DUG DANG 'DRES PA'I ZAS MNYAM DU ZOS NAS GCIG SHI GCIG SHI LA KHAD DU GYUR GCIG NA NAS YOD NA CIG SHOS MA NA PA DE LA 'GYOD PA GTAN MI BZOD PA 'ONG BA LTAR\", \"wylie\": \"rnam par sun 'byin pa'i stobs ni 'gyod sems byed pa ste dper na mi bzhis, dug dang 'dres pa'i zas mnyam du zos nas gcig shi gcig shi la khad du gyur gcig na nas yod na cig shos ma na pa de la 'gyod pa gtan mi bzod pa 'ong ba ltar\", \"english\": \"The \\\"power of destruction\\\" refers to an emotion of regret. Imagine for example that four people have been sitting around a table eating the same dish mixed with some deadly poison. Now one of them has already fallen over and died. Another is taking his last breath. The third is writhing in agony. The fourth hasn't started feeling the effects yet. Think though of the unbearable regret that he has already begun to feel about eating that particular dish.\", \"wylie_method\": \"glyph-decode\", \"decode_score\": 1.0}"
      },
      {
        "id": 9527,
        "course": "TCS02",
        "seq": 253,
        "acip": ",'GAG MED DU SNANG BA CHOS KYI DBYINGS, ,BDEN STONG DU 'CHAR BA SEMS KYI RGYUN, ,DBYER MED DU 'DRES PA'I RO GCIG PA, ,SEMS PA DE SEMS KYI RDO RJER SONG ,",
        "wylie": "'gag med du snang ba chos kyi dbyings, ,bden stong du 'char ba sems kyi rgyun, ,dbyer med du 'dres pa'i ro gcig pa, ,sems pa de sems kyi rdo rjer song",
        "english": "The never-ending flow Of the empty realm of all things Showed itself to me: The stream of my own thoughts, The revelation That there is nothing that's real. And then that thought Melted into the diamond of the mind, A single song Of their indivisible union.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"TCS02\", \"acip\": \",'GAG MED DU SNANG BA CHOS KYI DBYINGS, ,BDEN STONG DU 'CHAR BA SEMS KYI RGYUN, ,DBYER MED DU 'DRES PA'I RO GCIG PA, ,SEMS PA DE SEMS KYI RDO RJER SONG ,\", \"wylie\": \"'gag med du snang ba chos kyi dbyings, ,bden stong du 'char ba sems kyi rgyun, ,dbyer med du 'dres pa'i ro gcig pa, ,sems pa de sems kyi rdo rjer song\", \"english\": \"The never-ending flow Of the empty realm of all things Showed itself to me: The stream of my own thoughts, The revelation That there is nothing that's real. And then that thought Melted into the diamond of the mind, A single song Of their indivisible union.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 12709,
        "course": "TCS06",
        "seq": 526,
        "acip": "THIG LE DE RNAMS KYI NGO BO NI KHAMS DKAR DMAR 'DRES PA'I GONG BU YUNGS 'BRU TZAM PA RE YOD DO,,",
        "wylie": "thig le de rnams kyi ngo bo ni khams dkar dmar 'dres pa'i gong bu yungs 'bru tsam pa re yod do",
        "english": "The essential form of these drops is that each of them are little bits no larger than a mustard seed, in which the white and red elements are mixed together.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"TCS06\", \"acip\": \"THIG LE DE RNAMS KYI NGO BO NI KHAMS DKAR DMAR 'DRES PA'I GONG BU YUNGS 'BRU TZAM PA RE YOD DO,,\", \"wylie\": \"thig le de rnams kyi ngo bo ni khams dkar dmar 'dres pa'i gong bu yungs 'bru tsam pa re yod do\", \"english\": \"The essential form of these drops is that each of them are little bits no larger than a mustard seed, in which the white and red elements are mixed together.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 14424,
        "course": "TCS09",
        "seq": 195,
        "acip": "DE LA BDUD RTZI RIL BU DGOS KYANG, RNYING LUGS KYI RTZA BRGYAD STONG SBYAR ZHES PA SHA LNGA BDUD RTZI LNGA SOGS DNGOS SU 'DRES PA'I BDUD RTZI CHOS SMAN BSRE MI RUNG ZHING, 'DI DANG DGE LDAN PA'I BDUD RTZI RIL BU LA KHYAD PAR CHE STE, DGE LUGS LA SHA DANG BDUD RTZIR AA RU RA SOGS KYIS DOD THUB SBYAR BA YIN, SNGA MAS DNGOS SU BSRES PAS RANG GI RTOGS PAS MA 'CHUN NA NYES PA RLABS CHEN 'BYUNG BA'I NYEN YOD,",
        "wylie": "de la bdud rtsi ril bu dgos kyang, rnying lugs kyi rtsa brgyad stong sbyar zhes pa sha lnga bdud rtsi lnga sogs dngos su 'dres pa'i bdud rtsi chos sman bsre mi rung zhing, 'di dang dge ldan pa'i bdud rtsi ril bu la khyad par che ste, dge lugs la sha dang bdud rtsir aa ru ra sogs kyis dod thub sbyar ba yin, snga mas dngos su bsres pas rang gi rtogs pas ma 'chun na nyes pa rlabs chen 'byung ba'i nyen yod",
        "english": "For this practice you will need a nectar pill; but it is improper to mix together a dharma elixir like the \"Concoction of Eight Thousand Fundamental Substances\" used in the Nyingma tradition, where they add in the real things: the five fleshes, five nectars, and so on. There is a very great difference between this and the nectar pill of the Virtuous Ones.  In the tradition of the Way of Virtue, we mix together cherry plum and similar ingredients to substitute for the fleshes and nectars.  With the other custom, because you have blended in the actual substances, there is a very real danger that you will commit a tremendous bad deed if your realizations are not high enough to sustain the practice.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"TCS09\", \"acip\": \"DE LA BDUD RTZI RIL BU DGOS KYANG, RNYING LUGS KYI RTZA BRGYAD STONG SBYAR ZHES PA SHA LNGA BDUD RTZI LNGA SOGS DNGOS SU 'DRES PA'I BDUD RTZI CHOS SMAN BSRE MI RUNG ZHING, 'DI DANG DGE LDAN PA'I BDUD RTZI RIL BU LA KHYAD PAR CHE STE, DGE LUGS LA SHA DANG BDUD RTZIR AA RU RA SOGS KYIS DOD THUB SBYAR BA YIN, SNGA MAS DNGOS SU BSRES PAS RANG GI RTOGS PAS MA 'CHUN NA NYES PA RLABS CHEN 'BYUNG BA'I NYEN YOD,\", \"wylie\": \"de la bdud rtsi ril bu dgos kyang, rnying lugs kyi rtsa brgyad stong sbyar zhes pa sha lnga bdud rtsi lnga sogs dngos su 'dres pa'i bdud rtsi chos sman bsre mi rung zhing, 'di dang dge ldan pa'i bdud rtsi ril bu la khyad par che ste, dge lugs la sha dang bdud rtsir aa ru ra sogs kyis dod thub sbyar ba yin, snga mas dngos su bsres pas rang gi rtogs pas ma 'chun na nyes pa rlabs chen 'byung ba'i nyen yod\", \"english\": \"For this practice you will need a nectar pill; but it is improper to mix together a dharma elixir like the \\\"Concoction of Eight Thousand Fundamental Substances\\\" used in the Nyingma tradition, where they add in the real things: the five fleshes, five nectars, and so on. There is a very great difference between this and the nectar pill of the Virtuous Ones.  In the tradition of the Way of Virtue, we mix together cherry plum and similar ingredients to substitute for the fleshes and nectars.  With the other custom, because you have blended in the actual substances, there is a very real danger that you will commit a tremendous bad deed if your realizations are not high enough to sustain the practice.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 18426,
        "course": "TCS15",
        "seq": 283,
        "acip": "BSKYED RIM GSAL BAR BYED PA LA KHANG PA KHYAD PAR CAN BSGRUBS PA'I NANG DU, RDZAS SNA GZHAN MANG PO YANG TSOGS PAR BYAS NAS, BRIS SKU SOGS ME LONG GI NANG DU SHAR BA LA BLTAS KYIN SGOM PA CIG , MAR 'GOS GNYIS KA'I LUGS LA 'JUG PA DANG 'DRES PA'I RNAM GZHAG CIG 'BYUNG 'DUG GO,",
        "wylie": "bskyed rim gsal bar byed pa la khang pa khyad par can bsgrubs pa'i nang du, rdzas sna gzhan mang po yang tshogs par byas nas, bris sku sogs me long gi nang du shar ba la bltas kyin sgom pa cig , mar 'gos gnyis ka'i lugs la 'jug pa dang 'dres pa'i rnam gzhag cig 'byung 'dug go",
        "english": "We also find descriptions where, in order to clarify certain points on the stage of creation, one sets up a special room. Inside this room you set up a whole variety of objects, including paintings of holy beings and the like, which you get to reflect in mirrors. And then you teach the student to stare at the mirror and meditate that way. This is all some kind of mixed-up version of teachings that can be found in the systems of Lord Marpa and Gu.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"TCS15\", \"acip\": \"BSKYED RIM GSAL BAR BYED PA LA KHANG PA KHYAD PAR CAN BSGRUBS PA'I NANG DU, RDZAS SNA GZHAN MANG PO YANG TSOGS PAR BYAS NAS, BRIS SKU SOGS ME LONG GI NANG DU SHAR BA LA BLTAS KYIN SGOM PA CIG , MAR 'GOS GNYIS KA'I LUGS LA 'JUG PA DANG 'DRES PA'I RNAM GZHAG CIG 'BYUNG 'DUG GO,\", \"wylie\": \"bskyed rim gsal bar byed pa la khang pa khyad par can bsgrubs pa'i nang du, rdzas sna gzhan mang po yang tshogs par byas nas, bris sku sogs me long gi nang du shar ba la bltas kyin sgom pa cig , mar 'gos gnyis ka'i lugs la 'jug pa dang 'dres pa'i rnam gzhag cig 'byung 'dug go\", \"english\": \"We also find descriptions where, in order to clarify certain points on the stage of creation, one sets up a special room. Inside this room you set up a whole variety of objects, including paintings of holy beings and the like, which you get to reflect in mirrors. And then you teach the student to stare at the mirror and meditate that way. This is all some kind of mixed-up version of teachings that can be found in the systems of Lord Marpa and Gu.\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 18975,
        "course": "TCS16KaliWang",
        "seq": 194,
        "acip": "DE RNAMS SNYOMS PAR ZHUGS PA'I BYANG CHUB KYI SEMS DKAR DMAR 'DRES PA'I RGYUN SLOB MA'I SPYI BO NAS ZHUGS PAR MOS TE,",
        "wylie": "de rnams snyoms par zhugs pa'i byang chub kyi sems dkar dmar 'dres pa'i rgyun slob ma'i spyi bo nas zhugs par mos te",
        "english": "We watch as the Angels go into The meditation of union; A stream of the white And red elements mixed Flows in through the crowns Of the disciples' heads.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"TCS16KaliWang\", \"acip\": \"DE RNAMS SNYOMS PAR ZHUGS PA'I BYANG CHUB KYI SEMS DKAR DMAR 'DRES PA'I RGYUN SLOB MA'I SPYI BO NAS ZHUGS PAR MOS TE,\", \"wylie\": \"de rnams snyoms par zhugs pa'i byang chub kyi sems dkar dmar 'dres pa'i rgyun slob ma'i spyi bo nas zhugs par mos te\", \"english\": \"We watch as the Angels go into The meditation of union; A stream of the white And red elements mixed Flows in through the crowns Of the disciples' heads.\", \"repair_wave\": \"tcs2-v25-1\"}"
      },
      {
        "id": 19969,
        "course": "TCS17",
        "seq": 107,
        "acip": "BDE STONG NYID GOMS PAR BYAS PAS, MNGON SHES LNGA THOB CING, GZHAN YANG SROG DBU MAR 'DRES PA'I MTHUS RNAL 'BYOR PA RANG LA LHAN SKYES KHYAD PAR CAN STER BAS, SNA TSOGS YUM GYI BYA BA RNAMS KYANG BYED PAR 'GYUR RO,,",
        "wylie": "bde stong nyid goms par byas pas, mngon shes lnga thob cing, gzhan yang srog dbu mar 'dres pa'i mthus rnal 'byor pa rang la lhan skyes khyad par can ster bas, sna tshogs yum gyi bya ba rnams kyang byed par 'gyur ro",
        "english": "And if we accustom ourselves to this crucial practice of bliss and voidness, then we can attain the five forms of clairvoyance.  Moreover, the power imparted by bringing the life-wind to mix into the central channel grants the deep practitioner themselves an extraordinary form of simultaneous wisdom, which then allows them to perform the various activities of the Woman of Various Forms.",
        "raw": "{\"course\": \"TCS17\", \"acip\": \"BDE STONG NYID GOMS PAR BYAS PAS, MNGON SHES LNGA THOB CING, GZHAN YANG SROG DBU MAR 'DRES PA'I MTHUS RNAL 'BYOR PA RANG LA LHAN SKYES KHYAD PAR CAN STER BAS, SNA TSOGS YUM GYI BYA BA RNAMS KYANG BYED PAR 'GYUR RO,,\", \"wylie\": \"bde stong nyid goms par byas pas, mngon shes lnga thob cing, gzhan yang srog dbu mar 'dres pa'i mthus rnal 'byor pa rang la lhan skyes khyad par can ster bas, sna tshogs yum gyi bya ba rnams kyang byed par 'gyur ro\", \"english\": \"And if we accustom ourselves to this crucial practice of bliss and voidness, then we can attain the five forms of clairvoyance.  Moreover, the power imparted by bringing the life-wind to mix into the central channel grants the deep practitioner themselves an extraordinary form of simultaneous wisdom, which then allows them to perform the various activities of the Woman of Various Forms.\"}"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "sql": "select * from corpus_segments where wylie like ? order by course,seq",
